  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "3VsdrzofJWXC8kqi2AAUgIhcL1A=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The `DocumentToolbar` accepts a `toolbarClassName` prop for the outer container and a `controlsContainerClassName` prop for each controls container. There is no `className` prop. Both are merged with the component's default Tailwind classes using `twMerge`. The outer container defaults are:\n\n```\nflex h-12 w-full items-center justify-between rounded-xl border border-border bg-background px-4\n```\n\nTo override these defaults, you must use the `!` (important) prefix on your custom classes:\n\n```tsx\n<DocumentToolbar toolbarClassName=\"!bg-[#181825] !border-white/10\" />\n```\n\nWithout the `!` prefix, `twMerge` may resolve conflicts in favor of the defaults depending on specificity rules. The `!` prefix forces your values to take precedence.\n\nThis is a standard pattern when working with component libraries that use `twMerge` \u2014 the library controls base styling and consumers override specific properties via important modifiers. The same merge behavior applies to `controlsContainerClassName` and to the `className` prop on the individual toolbar buttons.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z"
    }
  },
